{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules","id":1048771,"title":"Gravity supremacy rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-14T09:08:30-08:00","id":1048771,"title":"Gravity supremacy rules","content":"Hi guys. Can you help me with this spell? Yesterday, during a tough fight, one of my pc used it. But I felt was a little OP: their enemy couldn't t just do nothing. Luckily, the fight was inside a room and the enemy could reach the ceiling and use it to jump in fight again. Anyway, I m gonna explain better.. First of all, a clarification : how much distance the gravity can be changed? <br /> As the range chosen? <br /> <br /> Going on: the spell has no withstand, no clash of wills. So, how do you manage to escape it? I mean, you can cast on a opponent and for the rest of duration he can t move unless he can use some surfaces to grab and jump over.. How do you manage this? <br /> Regards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:34:40-08:00","id":1048783,"title":"","content":"Mages are extremely good at cheesing things, it's just how their magic is. So yeah, if the person the mage was facing had no way of countering having gravity flipped on them then they're just out of luck. They could attempt to grab onto something, climb their way to the mage, or try to jump at them if applicable but that's just one of the difficulties of fighting a mage. <br /> <br /> The only advice I can really offer here is to always keep your players capabilities in mind when trying to design threatening enemies and to remember that the caster (unless using something that makes it so they are) isn't immune to their own effects. So if he reverses gravity in an entire room and he's also in said room, he reverses gravity for himself too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:37:24-08:00","id":1048784,"title":"","content":"Basic lesson of fighting a Mage on his terms -- Don't.<br /> <br /> Mages can screw over most opponents with a single spell. That's intentional. Mage (the game) isn't about &quot;can you win this fight?&quot;, it's about &quot;what are you willing to do to win this fight?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:37:37-08:00","id":1048785,"title":"","content":"Scale Factor determines how far gravity shifts extend. As for the combat problems it introduces, that's the whole point. Enemies who tangle with Mages have to be able to contend with the reality warping problems Mages can introduce them to. STs have to wrap their heads around that too.<br /> <br /> What were they fighting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:05:27-08:00","id":1048804,"title":"","content":"Another problem with those facing mages is the variety of abilities and lack of consistency among mages.<br /> <br /> It's very hard to train to fight mages, and an effective strategy in one battle is totally useless against the next mage.<br /> <br /> In one battle a mage may employ mind control and teleportation, another shapechanges, yet another alters probability, and then the next opponent nullifies gravity or shoots lightening. Trying to simultaneously combat a diverse and experienced cabal is often little more than suicide by wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:12:26-08:00","id":1048810,"title":"","content":"One thing you can do is exploit any lack of information. In Mage this isn't really unfair since Mages have the ability to find out nearly anything and a failure to do so is a flaw on the character's fault. If the Mages do their due diligence and find out everything they can about their opponent and prepare for it then they should trounce them. If they just jump into an unfamiliar situation without checking things out then you should feel free to add things that complicate the situation for them. As an ST this can require boning up on your ability to improvise. Remember, if it hasn't happened in front of the PCs then it isn't a fact and can change as you need it to in order to create a good story. Try not to be a dick about it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:57:57-08:00","id":1048982,"title":"","content":"Well.. They were fighting a werewolf.. Long story.. But maybe I missred the spell.. Can be cast on target only? Or it 's a aoe? ( in this case was the entire room,and was an error from my judgment). <br /> Anyway, thanks for answers. There are a lot of materials about thinking. I have only a bit of knowledge about werewolf, and we v just started recently playing mage. We played a lot of time vampire the masquerade, and, if the vampires were strong, I Donno how to paragon them to mages... Mages are simply OP.. Most of spells can blow up an entire strategy.. Space and time for example are gorgeous.. Force is amazing to create powerful spells ( controlling fire someone said) with amazing effects.. Disciplines can t just be compared to spell.. I must admit.. I m falling in love on this second edition of awakening<br /> <br /> BTW: one of the players reached 8 dice of paradox <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but was lucky.. Always absorbed with force of will.. But he used almost all mana <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12670,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","user":"Dante90","date":". 02-14-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:15:42-08:00","id":1049027,"title":"","content":"Gravity is exerted by large masses, you'd have to cast it over an area (Calculated by Scale) for it to have an effect, that's why there's no Withstand, sounds like it was a mistake on your part. No big, we all make them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:46:35-08:00","id":1049050,"title":"","content":"Oh... Well.. My bad.. But no great deal anyway. Good to know for the future of course. Thank you again guys. You really helped me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T02:09:43-08:00","id":1049191,"title":"","content":"It can be cast on an area around a target, but still. It's should be Withstood in this case. If for some reason you don't agree with this you can cast Shielding spell to ward your target from gravity and then just give him a little push to the atmosphere. Release the spell after half an hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T02:50:13-08:00","id":1049203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049191#post1049191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be cast on an area around a target, but still. It's should be Withstood in this case. If for some reason you don't agree with this you can cast Shielding spell to ward your target from gravity and then just give him a little push to the atmosphere. Release the spell after half an hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Withstand only comes into play when a spell is directly effecting a target. That's a deliberate design choice to push players to spells that don't just do direct damage. So no, casting Gravity Supremacy on an area doesn't deal with Withstand. The Shield against gravity would though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T02:53:45-08:00","id":1049204,"title":"","content":"I mean the case when you make a target a center point of an effect in this way that when it moves, the effect moves with it. I think it should be Withstood but I'm not arguing, it's a table thing I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:40:00-08:00","id":1049223,"title":"","content":"well, i have no problem adding a home rule like this, but i don t wanna go too far from the RAW..i just have the feel that they can resolve any task with this: let s gravity up while we flee, or retreat, or (worst) we killed him..i just don t wanna see an &quot;i win strategy&quot;, and maybe adding some counterplay could be nice.<br /> i forgot to write, but in case wasn t clear, we r playing at the second edition<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:59:55-08:00","id":1049234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049203#post1049203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Withstand only comes into play when a spell is directly effecting a target. That's a deliberate design choice to push players to spells that don't just do direct damage. So no, casting Gravity Supremacy on an area doesn't deal with Withstand. The Shield against gravity would though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get what you are saying, but I find this specific case funny because Direct Damage spells don't involve Withstand, ever. And yeah, Mage is designed towards cheesing your opponents in a first move hoping they won't find an answer to your cheese that can both nullify your cheese while also cheesing you. In general, person with better Initiative and more guts to not pull their punches wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:21:22-08:00","id":1049245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049234#post1049234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you are saying, but I find this specific case funny because Direct Damage spells don't involve Withstand, ever. And yeah, Mage is designed towards cheesing your opponents in a first move hoping they won't find an answer to your cheese that can both nullify your cheese while also cheesing you. In general, person with better Initiative and more guts to not pull their punches wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stamina is counted as the Withstand in direct damage spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:54:42-08:00","id":1049256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049245#post1049245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stamina is counted as the Withstand in direct damage spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only to the extent that Stamina is already accounted for in your Health level. Stamina does not reduce Potency levels of damage per attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:41:41-08:00","id":1049330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049223#post1049223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, i have no problem adding a home rule like this, but i don t wanna go too far from the RAW..i just have the feel that they can resolve any task with this: let s gravity up while we flee, or retreat, or (worst) we killed him..i just don t wanna see an &amp;quot;i win strategy&amp;quot;, and maybe adding some counterplay could be nice.<br /> i forgot to write, but in case wasn t clear, we r playing at the second edition</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't something limited just to Gravitic Supremacy. You can manage the same shenanigans with Space 3s Ban or Matter 3s State Change and probably quite a few others.<br /> <br /> The simple fact of the matter is that you're going to need to think creatively when dealing with mages. If you find your group continually relying on a single or handful of strategies then you'll need to send things after them capable of dealing with those strategies and force them to think outside the box. <br /> <br /> If they keep flipping gravity, use enemies proficient in fighting at range, or who can comfortably fight as well in the air as they can on the ground. Maybe enemies that can generate platforms or enemies that can stick to walls. Yes, there are some enemies that simply have no response to this sort of thing and that's OK. Yes, they get hosed but that's the upside of being a mage and playing to your strengths. It's an intended part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:57:36-08:00","id":1049339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049204#post1049204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the case when you make a target a center point of an effect in this way that when it moves, the effect moves with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a thing. Gravitic Supremacy alters the gravity in a defined area, not a mobile radius around an individual target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049234#post1049234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, person with better Initiative and more guts to not pull their punches wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words: Yes, the Guardians <i>do</i> have a point, because that shit makes you a magnet for trouble one way or another. Either you're rocking low Wisdom or you're dealing with the Mana demands of reshaping your magical identity to better permit you to end people or you've gone full Nefandi.<br /> <br /> <i>Something's</i> going to get you eventually. It's just a matter of what and when.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:42:36-08:00","id":1049365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049330#post1049330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't something limited just to Gravitic Supremacy. You can manage the same shenanigans with Space 3s Ban or Matter 3s State Change and probably quite a few others.<br /> <br /> The simple fact of the matter is that you're going to need to think creatively when dealing with mages. If you find your group continually relying on a single or handful of strategies then you'll need to send things after them capable of dealing with those strategies and force them to think outside the box.<br /> <br /> If they keep flipping gravity, use enemies proficient in fighting at range, or who can comfortably fight as well in the air as they can on the ground. Maybe enemies that can generate platforms or enemies that can stick to walls. Yes, there are some enemies that simply have no response to this sort of thing and that's OK. Yes, they get hosed but that's the upside of being a mage and playing to your strengths. It's an intended part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side note: If the all beings in conflict with the players have to specifically be able to grab or be in arms reach to provide the need for a dramatic solution, then there is something terribly wrong. Puzzles, mysteries, social intrigue/manuevering and physical confrontations that require things as exotic as a &quot;firearms&quot; (FYI:They shoot bullets) totally are not circumvented by altering gravity. If the players found a way to avoid a very specific type of scene, like chase scenes that require their chasers to follow a path which can be blocked by the area of a spell (Pretty specific) they should be rewarded, but if they use that trick more than a couple times odds are others will hear about it, and at very least that specific foe will be made aware of that tactic and move to counter it next time. PCs are not the only one to learn in the game, and having NPC react to PCs make the PC's action matter all the more.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As in Dresden Files <i>Changes</i>, where a long range rifle shot gets around the mage's ability to cast a death curse. Don't know who to target means you can't cast the spell, and being too far away to notice does that. Or as in the Anime <i>Fate/Zero</i> and the use of surprise roadside mundane bombs against magic users to avoid having to deal with arcane duels against more potent mages. Also the out of the box strategies used in TV series, <i>Break Bad</i>, such as explosive crystals that look like meth, using thermite to melt locks, dissolving bodies in barrels of acid, lethal poisons and so on; I mean just picture Walter White against a mage after the first confrontation and he saw what they can do. Not pretty.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-15-2017, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:10:23-08:00","id":1049415,"title":"","content":"Did the werewolf in question survive this encounter?<br /> <br /> Being prepared against Mages is crucial, and if the wolfie lived, the wolfie can come back with a pack. And they know this spell is something that can/will be used.<br /> They prepare grappling hooks for grounding and firearms or at least throwing weapons, only engage in closed spaces where they can use prodigious strength to literally jump at Mages from the ceiling if it comes to that (grapple rules maybe? Mages don't like those)<br /> <br /> And that's just for those specific ones. As others said, if they use the trick too much, word gets around, and then it's more reasonable that countermeasures are prepared.<br /> <br /> If there are consequences from this wolfie encounter (i.e. their allies approach) make the encounter in a public space, so shooting random passers-by into the air will be a risk. This provides choices (yes they can launch a whole plaza into the air, that brings a whole new set of issues)<br /> <br /> If your players like combat challenges, consider using environmental factors to provoke interesting creative spellcasting - in darkness, in a heavily-treed area with attacks from above as well as maneuvers behind trees and such. In an office building with corridors twisting and creating ambush possibilities. Both of those environments can involve lighting circumstances as well as provide interesting reactions to the gravity trick - swing off branches even if you're falling upwards, use added momentum, some office building corridors have low ceilings, barely a jump to engage into melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:16:04-08:00","id":1049416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049339#post1049339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a thing. Gravitic Supremacy alters the gravity in a defined area, not a mobile radius around an individual target.<br /> <br /> In other words: Yes, the Guardians <i>do</i> have a point, because that shit makes you a magnet for trouble one way or another. Either you're rocking low Wisdom or you're dealing with the Mana demands of reshaping your magical identity to better permit you to end people or you've gone full Nefandi.<br /> <br /> <i>Something's</i> going to get you eventually. It's just a matter of what and when.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything can be cast on an area or the target. Those are basics of spellcasting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:25:09-08:00","id":1049422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049416#post1049416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything can be cast on an area or the target. Those are basics of spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Co-Location begs to differ. Also, neither of those things are &quot;Every spell can be made into a mixed-Scale roving AoE.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:25:31-08:00","id":1049423,"title":"","content":"The easiest counter in this case, would have been to bring a gun, because over short distance, gravity isn't going to do much to stop a bullet without the Mage taking drastic measures.<br /> <br /> Gravitic Supremacy, and Gravity Control can of course be cast on individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:36:41-08:00","id":1049426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049423#post1049423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gravitic Supremacy, and Gravity Control can of course be cast on individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the effect would be negligible (Non-mechanical effect), since a normal person or even a werewolf in full Gauru doesn't exert much gravity in the first place. It also wouldn't be able to make the target fall up because the gravity of earth would still be greater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:59:35-08:00","id":1049515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049339#post1049339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a thing. Gravitic Supremacy alters the gravity in a defined area, not a mobile radius around an individual target.<br /> <br /> In other words: Yes, the Guardians <i>do</i> have a point, because that shit makes you a magnet for trouble one way or another. Either you're rocking low Wisdom or you're dealing with the Mana demands of reshaping your magical identity to better permit you to end people or you've gone full Nefandi.<br /> <br /> <i>Something's</i> going to get you eventually. It's just a matter of what and when.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't see why something like that couldn't be done as either conjunctional or combined spell involving Forces and Space. Or even just Forces itself with some sort of vector control or telekinetic effect added in. Obviously this seems to be something like a 3 dot spell and not something like actually flipping gravity which sounds like making/unmaking to me. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-15-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:13:34-08:00","id":1049520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049515#post1049515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI don't see why something like that couldn't be done as either conjunctional or combined spell involving Forces and Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sole precedents involved are a pair of spells that are specifically designed around attracting or repelling particular phenomena to or from the subject, neither of which scans to a mobile sphere of altered gravity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:18:27-08:00","id":1049523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049515#post1049515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI don't see why something like that couldn't be done as either conjunctional or combined spell involving Forces and Space. Or even just Forces itself with some sort of vector control or telekinetic effect added in. Obviously this seems to be something like a 3 dot spell and not something like actually flipping gravity which sounds like making/unmaking to me. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049426#post1049426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">True, but the effect would be negligible (Non-mechanical effect), since a normal person or even a werewolf in full Gauru doesn't exert much gravity in the first place. It also wouldn't be able to make the target fall up because the gravity of earth would still be greater.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I repeat myself.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:22:28-08:00","id":1049524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049520#post1049520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sole precedents involved are a pair of spells that are specifically designed around attracting or repelling particular phenomena to or from the subject, neither of which scans to a mobile sphere of altered gravity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's not the question. I see no reason it shouldn't be possible to design a spell or a combined spell more exactly to affect both gravity and vector of an area with exclusion of at least yourself. This is just if you don't have the capability to either just outright remove or reverse gravity which this spell doesn't seem to be designed to do. It just seems to alter not wholesale change the properties of gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-15-2017, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:59:20-08:00","id":1049540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049422#post1049422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Co-Location begs to differ. Also, neither of those things are &amp;quot;Every spell can be made into a mixed-Scale roving AoE.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What stops you to cast it on two items to have e.g. cellphone-sword that you can switch reflexively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:06:04-08:00","id":1049590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049540#post1049540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What stops you to cast it on two items to have e.g. cellphone-sword that you can switch reflexively?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you can't teleport objects into other objects with it, the fact that the nearest thing to a swap within the spell is two separate reflexive &quot;movements,&quot; and the fact that <i>actually</i> switching the places of two objects with Space is a function of Teleportation that doesn't work on objects of substantially different Sizes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T21:17:52-08:00","id":1049681,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>'s point on spells existing that only affect areas works nicely for colocation.<br /> <br /> However, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, I would say it's just because the text of the spell explicitly talks about subjects and those &quot;caught in the area,&quot; going for plural all the time. I don't think it unreasonable to allow it (or a creatively thaumaturgised spell) to target an individual, because while it is true what you say, that the werewolf's exertion of gravity is negligible, same holds true for anything you can reasonably hope to catch in the spell's area.<br /> nless you are forced to up the scale to encompass a really significant portion of the Earth, anything else will exert negligible amounts of gravity.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, physics is iffy for magic. Just make the 10m/s\u02c72 we generally think of as gravity work into a chosen direction for the target. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T00:49:23-08:00","id":1049736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049590#post1049590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you can't teleport objects into other objects with it, the fact that the nearest thing to a swap within the spell is two separate reflexive &amp;quot;movements,&amp;quot; and the fact that <i>actually</i> switching the places of two objects with Space is a function of Teleportation that doesn't work on objects of substantially different Sizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a function of Teleportation. Function of Teleportation is to swap targets with a spell. Difference between 3rd and 4th dot is a number of steps. Co-location bind targets an then allows you to swap them while Teleportation swaps them in a single motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T01:34:08-08:00","id":1049746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049681#post1049681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s point on spells existing that only affect areas works nicely for colocation.<br /> <br /> However, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I would say it's just because the text of the spell explicitly talks about subjects and those &amp;quot;caught in the area,&amp;quot; going for plural all the time. I don't think it unreasonable to allow it (or a creatively thaumaturgised spell) to target an individual, because while it is true what you say, that the werewolf's exertion of gravity is negligible, same holds true for anything you can reasonably hope to catch in the spell's area.<br /> nless you are forced to up the scale to encompass a really significant portion of the Earth, anything else will exert negligible amounts of gravity.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, physics is iffy for magic. Just make the 10m/s\u02c72 we generally think of as gravity work into a chosen direction for the target. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gravity forces inside an area are being exerted at a constant rate from the earth, you're manipulating that. I'm not talking about mixing physics and magic except in the most abstract sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T01:38:16-08:00","id":1049747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049415#post1049415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the werewolf in question survive this encounter?<br /> <br /> Being prepared against Mages is crucial, and if the wolfie lived, the wolfie can come back with a pack. And they know this spell is something that can/will be used.<br /> They prepare grappling hooks for grounding and firearms or at least throwing weapons, only engage in closed spaces where they can use prodigious strength to literally jump at Mages from the ceiling if it comes to that (grapple rules maybe? Mages don't like those)<br /> <br /> And that's just for those specific ones. As others said, if they use the trick too much, word gets around, and then it's more reasonable that countermeasures are prepared.<br /> <br /> If there are consequences from this wolfie encounter (i.e. their allies approach) make the encounter in a public space, so shooting random passers-by into the air will be a risk. This provides choices (yes they can launch a whole plaza into the air, that brings a whole new set of issues)<br /> <br /> If your players like combat challenges, consider using environmental factors to provoke interesting creative spellcasting - in darkness, in a heavily-treed area with attacks from above as well as maneuvers behind trees and such. In an office building with corridors twisting and creating ambush possibilities. Both of those environments can involve lighting circumstances as well as provide interesting reactions to the gravity trick - swing off branches even if you're falling upwards, use added momentum, some office building corridors have low ceilings, barely a jump to engage into melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>firsti of all, disclaimer: love this community!! you all are so nice!!<br /> <br /> move on: settings is london 1817, the werewolf fight wasn t supposed to kill the party, but the battle was a starting point for more plots ( why a werewolf was beneath the oxford cemetery?? why didn t have a pack?? and so on)<br /> An ally of PC was there to help if needed, and yes, without him, they probabily died, but just because they have no much experience in mage the awakening, a little of missplay from their part, but i m pretty sure they could have easily won the fight..<br /> <br /> anyway, what i need to unerstand, is if by RAW i can cast this spell on a target, or, i 'll cast the spell like an area of effect of the appropriate scale/dimension of the target size<br /> so, for example, to cast gravity on a werewolf (trasformed, so size 6), i need to cast as second level on the scale table, that has dimension of a small room ( i m gonna assume 4x4 square room). In this case the absence of withdraw is understandable cause also the caster will be hit by his own spell<br /> <br /> but from now on, their enemies know their arcana ( they use death, space, time and force).. in the end, after more than 10 years playing D&amp;D i know how give problems to my players.. i wanna just know if i have understand the rule <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:54:00-08:00","id":1049845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049746#post1049746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gravity forces inside an area are being exerted at a constant rate from the earth, you're manipulating that. I'm not talking about mixing physics and magic except in the most abstract sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. But in a way I want to elaborate more on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Gravity is attraction between two objects, depends on both of their mass and the distance between them.<br /> So any given two objects attract one another by means of gravity. These forces are often negligible, so we only count the attraction of Earth to everything else when saying &quot;gravity&quot; in everyday speech.<br /> <br /> Depending on they way you want to look at this, it can be either 1) &quot;the Earth attracts everything, and in this spell's area that force changes direction &quot; or it can be 2) &quot;the Earth attracts this object and this spell changes the direction of that force&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12670\" data-vbnamecard=\"12670\">Dante90</a> As far as Gravitic Supremacy goes, the lack of a Withstand is enough of an implication that it's meant to affect an area.<br /> <br /> But that's why we have Creative Thaumaturgy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I never understood really, in any setting where telekinesis is conveniently easy to do and maintain, how any telekineticist can lose to anyone who has to close into melee range to fight ... just lift them a few cm off the ground and leave them there, win)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:02:59-08:00","id":1049878,"title":"","content":"Yep, as written Gravitic Supremacy works on an area, but since Creative Thaumaturgy is a thing, you can easily change that by coming up with a similar spell designed to center the effect on individuals. It would of course be Withstood, but that's the price you pay when you want the added accuracy of directly targeting someone's pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:42:00-08:00","id":1049896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049590#post1049590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you can't teleport objects into other objects with it, the fact that the nearest thing to a swap within the spell is two separate reflexive &amp;quot;movements,&amp;quot; and the fact that <i>actually</i> switching the places of two objects with Space is a function of Teleportation that doesn't work on objects of substantially different Sizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The substantially different size problem is one solved by proper use of scale, teleportation is already mentioned in colocation, swapping has nothing to do with targeting objects/people if you're colocating empty air and those objects/people, and the clause of preventing objects from being teleported inside each other is to clearly delineate the spell from collapse. You can DEFINITELY colocate objects/people. You just have to be clever about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:54:06-08:00","id":1049905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049896#post1049896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The substantially different size problem is one solved by proper use of scale, teleportation is already mentioned in colocation, swapping has nothing to do with targeting objects/people if you're colocating empty air and those objects/people, and the clause of preventing objects from being teleported inside each other is to clearly delineate the spell from collapse. You can DEFINITELY colocate objects/people. You just have to be clever about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;empty air&quot; <i>inside another object</i>, which is <i>the only space that exists in a version of Co-Location that does not target an area.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:56:19-08:00","id":1049906,"title":"","content":"Unless you colocate an object and a location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:00:49-08:00","id":1049908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049906#post1049906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you colocate an object and a location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither a sword nor a cellular phone is a location and colocating a location <i>definitionally is not a version of Co-Location that does not target an area</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm not contesting the theoretical existence of a Space spell with the capacity to swap objects, I'm saying <i>the Co-Location spell is not a spell for swapping objects</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:05:11-08:00","id":1049911,"title":"","content":"Given the fact that Space says distance is a lie, all points are one, I'd disagree with the assertion that objects and people aren't locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:28:56-08:00","id":1049922,"title":"","content":"wow guys.. you r totally going on a phylosophical argumentations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> there are diferent points of view through the thread..<br /> didn t understand how you menage this &quot;kind&quot; of spell thou.. my interpretation stands still.. for the love of simplicity i'll rule it how i said earlier: can t be casted on target, but an aoe, with a radius of the appropriated level in the scale table ( base on the enemy's size)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:01:53-08:00","id":1050191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048771-gravity-supremacy-rules?p=1049878#post1049878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, as written Gravitic Supremacy works on an area, but since Creative Thaumaturgy is a thing, you can easily change that by coming up with a similar spell designed to center the effect on individuals. It would of course be Withstood, but that's the price you pay when you want the added accuracy of directly targeting someone's pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's exactly what I am trying to get across it should be very possible to use gravity as something targeted. I expect nothing less then it to be withstood. Any decent amount of Forces already allows for other types of energy (kinetic for example) to be targeted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-16-2017, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","